# src/apps/daemon/internal/runtime/proxy

## Purpose
Primary evasion and proxy-qualification runtime. Owns evasion lifecycle/dialing/transports plus Xray/sing-box qualification; mobile platform/runtime, safety, trust, routing-provider policy, and decoy traffic are separate owners.

## Architectural role
- Daemon dependency band: `runtime` (rank 4; lower rank = deeper implementation).
- Cross-band imports may point only to a lower rank. Same-band imports are allowed when they remain within one architectural layer.

## Contents
- Direct files (155): `accept_backoff.go`, `accept_backoff_test.go`, `adaptive_dialer.go`, `adaptive_dialer_test.go`, `auto_reconnect.go`, `brook_codec.go`, `brook_codec_test.go`, `brook_transport.go`, `brook_transport_test.go`, `circular_cache.go`, `circular_cache_test.go`, `config_watcher.go` …

## Interfaces and dependencies
- Go package: `proxy`.
- Notable exported surface: `AdaptiveDialer`, `AddDiagnosticTrace`, `AggregatedFlow`, `AndroidVPNExclusionManager`, `AtomicNoizeWireGuardConn`, `BetterEndpointQuality`, `BrookCodec`, `BrookConn`, `BrookRequest`, `BrookTargetType` …
- Daemon-local dependencies: `internal/foundation/boundedio`, `internal/foundation/config`, `internal/foundation/crypto`, `internal/foundation/flowregistry`, `internal/foundation/remoteaction`, `internal/foundation/trafficstats`, `internal/integrations/relayclient`, `internal/native/bridge`, `internal/networking/geoip`, `internal/networking/kcppolicy`, `internal/networking/proxyconfig`, `internal/networking/tlsdecoy`, `internal/platform/mobilehost`, `internal/platform/process`, `internal/platform/sshtrust`, `internal/platform/system`, `internal/protocols/asyncreactor`, `internal/protocols/tlsfragment`, `internal/runtime/trust`.
- Direct daemon callers: `cmd`, `internal/adapters/api`, `internal/runtime/mobilecore`, `internal/workflows/jobs`.

## Invariants
- Evasion configuration/defaulting/redaction/lifecycle stay owned by the evasion runtime.
- Xray/sing-box qualification is ephemeral and remains separate from long-lived runtimecore engines.
- `runtime` code must not import a higher-rank daemon band.

